  "id": "Compound::DB00921 - Gene::4985",
  "verbalization": "Buprenorphine is strongly associated with Oprd1 through multiple integrated pathways, suggesting a role in opioid receptor activation. The evidence indicates that Buprenorphine binds to Oprl1, which is a key component in the opioid receptor pathway, and that this binding is linked to opioid receptor activity. This mechanism is further supported by the inclusion of Buprenorphine in the class of partial opioid agonists, which includes compounds like Butorphanol and Pentazocine, all of which are known to interact with Oprd1. The shared lowest common ancestors between Buprenorphine and these compounds point to a common pathway involving the opioid system, reinforcing the notion that Buprenorphine exerts its effects through Oprd1. The integrated evidence suggests that Buprenorphine modulates opioid receptor activity via Oprd1, contributing to its analgesic effects while also highlighting the broader context of opioid receptor engagement.",
